      "longDescription": "MORRO is a self-branding exercise.\n\nAfter years of putting it off and a couple of failed attempts, I finally figured out my own visual identity. Those earlier attempts taught me that meaning wasn't enough; I also needed a style that actually felt like me. After a lot of research, sketching and testing, that turned out to be imperfect but clean design, relaxed shapes, warm tones and everyday imagery.\n\nSketches turned into digital vectors, then got mixed with texture, type, color and photography. What you'll see in the gallery is the result.\n\nAfter this, it was time to build the website around the new identity. Moodboards, sketches, code tests and some early AI pair-coding got me a rough first version. Claude Code later helped me rebuild it properly: a front-end, plus a simple back-end I manage through GitHub, so I'm not stuck depending on AI just to keep the site running.\n\nThanks for reading.",
