      "longDescription": "Gestión Reaviva provides technical services for construction projects. This project was a redesign of their visual identity and website, both untouched for over a decade and no longer reflecting the company's pivot from real estate to technical services.\n\nThe client gave full freedom on the rebrand, since the old identity wasn't well recognised. Early meetings led to a key call: update the naming itself. The new logotype reads \"Gestión Reaviva,\" the company's full name, emphasizing the services they actually offer. I adjusted an existing typeface's details and kerning, and added custom letters that became the brand's isotype. The new identity rolled out across business cards and office materials, and set the direction for the website.\n\nFor the site, the brief was clear: rework the architecture for clarity, and build it on a CMS so the client could update it themselves, no custom backend needed. I redesigned the structure and user flow around that, resulting in a home page, clean menu, structured galleries and a clear contact page.",
